s of $t$ where the curve $x=t+6,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-4$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-1$ are $t=-3$ and $t=4.$" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342128 13194139535291 true] [17592186342127 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535291 true] [17592186342127 1041 "field-1" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342127 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342128 13194139535291 true] [17592186342127 1110 #uuid "ab80bea9-201d-5742-aad6-fc6eeeb9bfc7" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342128 1034 "-3" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535291 true] [17592186342128 1111 #uuid "435ff245-ff47-5939-ae21-4ea4d0a92b25" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342130 13194139535291 true] [17592186342129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535291 true] [17592186342129 1041 "field-2" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342130 13194139535291 true] [17592186342129 1110 #uuid "24a0e711-94c0-58a4-a8ce-787bad8b43a7" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342130 1034 "4" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535291 true] [17592186342130 1111 #uuid "e9297d38-5550-5b27-9cfb-335af5980727" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342132 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342135 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342137 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1089 "q-274673" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1100 "Find the points where the curve $x={t}^{2},\\,y=4t$ intersects the line $x+y+3=0.$\n\nThe intersection points are $(1,$\n{{field-1}}$)$ and $(${{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$).$" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1113 #uuid "dbb7e394-0cf1-5a5c-a310-9a9d31edc44a" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342131 1145 "To find the coordinates of intersection points, we take the equation of the line, replace $x$ and $y$ with the parametric formulas, and then solve for $t.$ Upon finding $t,$ we then find the coordinates of the intersection points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+3 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}+4t+3 & =0 \\\\ (t+3)(t+1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we have the values of $t,$ we proceed to find $x$ and $y:$ \n\n- We start with $t=-3.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2} \\\\  & =(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4t \\\\  & =4(-3) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the first intersection point are $(9,-12).$\n\n- We now move over to $t=-1.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4t \\\\  & =4(-1) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the second intersection point are $(1,-4).$\n\nTherefore, the curve $x={t}^{2},y=4t$ intersects the line $x+y+3=0$ at the points $(1,-4)$ and $(9,-12).$" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342133 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342134 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1041 "field-1" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342133 13194139535291 true] [17592186342132 1110 #uuid "6cddf78a-4b10-581b-b222-be57730f9a28" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342133 1034 "-4" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535291 true] [17592186342133 1111 #uuid "e97f438d-0294-501a-8248-3306ad8af745" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342134 1034 "4" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535291 true] [17592186342134 1111 #uuid "2c57436f-bc5d-502c-96e6-6d12543d5e8e" 13194139535291 true] [17592186342135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342136 13194139535291 true] [17592186342135 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535291 true] [17592186342135 1041 "field-2" 13194139535291 true] [1759218